{
  "about": "The genex facade's agent-facing vocabularies, held by native/genex-rust/crates/genex/tests/vocabulary.rs (RUNTIME_KEYS, InstallErrorCode, the gpu_pass registration code, the Level-2 calls, which call each [[wgsl]] kind feeds, and the frame calls temporal effects need: draw ids and camera cuts; the environment calls with the wire spellings of its kinds and of `HdriSun`; the local-light and emissive calls of RQ6; the look's fog calls, A.5's volumetric opt-out among them; the calls that build a world's look: reflection probes and irradiance volumes, decals, grading and white balance, the lens, the night sky and subsurface) and read by tests/conformance/rust-template-docs.test.ts, which checks the template docs name each. Change both sides with this file. Its `meshlets` block is the renderer's `genex_meshlets` glTF extras schema (genex-render's meshlet.rs, the host's src/shared/render-quality.ts), held by vocabulary.rs and tests/conformance/genex-toml.test.ts. Its `animation`, `stream`, `nav`, `input`, `saves`, `ui`, `audio`, `profile`, `assets`, `lod`, `settings` and `net` blocks are the game systems' calls and refusals, empty until each area pins what works (`assets` is pinned: SF-1a's sim-side reads; `animation` holds the rig importer's, the graph builder's, the ragdoll's and the character controller's refusals and the animation surface's calls (AN-15); `stream` holds the cell grid's; `nav` holds the bake input's (collider input among them), the tile bake's and the off-mesh links' refusals, `frame.lines` and `frame.nav_debug`; `input` holds the action map's, the bindings file's, the journal's and the touch controls' refusals; `saves` holds the saves page's calls, genex-save's refusals, the volatile issue and the slot states and ops (UIS-9); `lod` holds a model's levels, bias and compounds and their refusals (LOD-07); `settings` holds the settings menu's calls and refusals (UIS-11); `ui` holds the ui page's calls, genex-ui's text refusals and its issue codes (UIS-10, held by vocabulary.rs and ui.rs); `audio` holds the audio page's calls and genex-audio's refusals (AU-9); `profile` holds the profiling page's calls and `volatile.profile`'s shape (PROF-5); `net` holds the net page's calls (MP-4b), `sim.net`'s local refusals (MP-4a) and the `__net` view's mode, status and offline-reason spellings, which src/shared/game-net.ts restates for Live's net row (MP-7, held by tests/conformance/net-row.test.ts)). Its `textures` block is the importer's `genex_textures` GLB extras schema (glb-textures.ts), held by tests/conformance/genex-toml.test.ts; C-14 pins the Rust reader against it in vocabulary.rs. Its `runtimeRender` block is __render's display-only texture facts (C-11): the keys, the family spellings and the asset issue codes.",
